course: dictionary
lesson: 11768
title: Barren
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Barren means so poor that nothing can grow. Look for clues around the word. «Nothing grew on the barren hill, only grey stones and dust.» Nothing grew, there were only stones and dust, so barren must mean bare and empty, with no plants.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «Nothing grew on the poor, empty hill» still makes sense, so you have got it right.
explain: Barren can also mean giving no results. «The meeting was barren: nobody agreed and nothing was decided.» Nothing was decided, so barren means it got nowhere. The clues tell you which meaning fits.
fact: «Barren» means too poor to grow plants or crops, like a barren desert.
fact: A «barren» tree is one that does not produce fruit.
fact: «Barren» can also mean empty and giving no results, like a barren argument.
fact: Barren deserts, ice fields and rocky islands are often called barren in geography and science.
fact: Context clues, like nothing grew or nothing was decided, help you find the right meaning.
exercise: «The barren desert had no water and no plants.» What does barren mean here? | *Too poor to grow plants | Very wet and cold | Full of green grass | Busy with farmers
exercise: «The old apple tree was barren, so it gave no apples this year.» What does barren mean? | Full of birds | Very tall | Covered in flowers | *Not producing fruit
exercise: «The talks were barren: nobody agreed, and nothing was decided.» What does barren suggest? | *Giving no results | Happily finished | Full of fun | Very noisy
test: «The ice field was barren, with nothing but snow and rock for miles.» What is the best meaning of barren here? | Covered in flowers | Full of animals | *Bare, with nothing able to grow | Warm and sunny
test: Which sentence uses barren to mean empty, with no results? | «The rocky island was barren.» | *«The brainstorm was barren: we had no ideas at all.» | «The desert was barren of plants.» | «The apple tree was barren of fruit.»
exam: Which word could replace barren in «The land was barren» and keep the same meaning? | soft | *bare and empty | crowded | bright
